HST Office: the Sheets ribbon takes the layout of the approved 1.0.2 mockup (hinh-mau-sheets.html, owner 15/11/2026).

Home: Clipboard is a large Paste beside a 3-row column of labelled Cut, Copy and Format Paintbrush (Paste Special
is in Paste's ▾ menu, so its separate button goes); Font is two rows (font, size, grow/shrink, clear formatting /
B I U S, sub- and superscript, border, fill and font colour); Styles is Conditional Formatting ▾, Format as
Table and the cell styles gallery (.uno:StylesPreview, which shows Calc's cell styles with
hst-ribbon-mockup-gallery-combos.patch) at the large size and a large Cell Styles ▾ (now with an icon) at
the medium and small sizes (owner decision 16/11/2026; the ladder shows one or the other); Alignment drops the hidden right-to-left and
left-to-right buttons (owner decision) and puts Decrease Indent before Increase Indent; Cells and Editing
fill three rows (AutoSum ▾, a column of Fill ▾ and Clear ▾, Sort and Filter ▾, Find and Select ▾). Insert: Charts
is Chart (the wizard) large, then icon-only drop-downs per chart family as in the reference suite (Column or Bar,
Line or Area, Pie or Doughnut, Scatter or Bubble, Stock or Radar, Combo; only types the chart wizard offers, so
no Hierarchy, Statistic, Waterfall, Funnel, Surface, Maps or PivotChart), each item opening the wizard on that chart
type (.uno:InsertObjectChart with a chart2 template name; fuins2.cxx accepts those names, and Calc's own
definition of the slot in tabvwsh.sdi now declares the ChartType argument, which the dispatcher dropped before), with the colibre
chart-type icons, and Sparkline large; Text is Text Box and Header and
Footer large beside two 3-row columns (Fontwork, Signature Line, Object / Vertical Text, Date, Time). Extensions
groups the HST tools as the mockup does: Text (administrative document, Remove Diacritics, Split Name, Sort by
Given Name), Vietnamese Formats (VND, date, percent), Data (Import CSV, Delete Blank Rows), Vietnamese Tools
(Number to Words, Convert Encoding), HASON TECH (Solutions, USB Token setup). Data ▸ Data Tools has Text to Columns
large beside the other tools, Review ▸ Comments has Delete large and View ▸ Window has New Window
large, as in the reference suite. Every other tab: large buttons fill
the three rows and small buttons stand in even 3-row columns (the mockup's grid()), captions under the rows,
separators 4 rows high. The ribbon's root box has no margin above, below or right of it and the tabs' group boxes no margin above or
below them, as in the other apps, so the separators and captions sit at the same height.
Every group keeps its id (the adaptive ladders apply); every command keeps its KeyTip (Cell Styles ▾ keeps J, which the
regenerated KeyTip table also gives to the gallery); the chart drop-downs are keyed by widget id
(btnHstInsertChartColumn, ...Line, ...Pie, ...Scatter, ...Other, ...Combo) for the reference letters C, N1, Q, D, I1, SD. Needs hst-ribbon-mockup-gallery-combos.patch before it.

